In a development related to the auto industry, the Thai Federation of Automobile Manufacturers reported over the weekend that the industry's exports fell to a 25-month low in December due to the slump. Domestic car orders, sales volume, car output and company profits, especially manufacturers, are concerned about the current political crisis.
Retailers call for renegotiation
Six major retailers, the Footwear and Garment Industry Association, whose members account for more than 90 per cent of US and Canadian garment exports, have called on the Cambodian government, the Cambodian Garment Manufacturers Association and key unions to return to the table. Negotiate again.
The letter states:
In addition to urging the immediate resumption of negotiations, the signatories are calling for the establishment of a regular wage setting mechanism and calling on all parties involved to end all violence.
The six executives who signed the letter were from the Canadian Retail Council, the American Clothing and Footwear Association, the American Fashion Industry Association, the Canadian Garment Federation, the Canadian Retail Industry Leaders Association and the National Retail Federation.
The call comes after factory workers went on strike demanding a $ 160 minimum wage and were subjected to a bloody crackdown that left five workers dead, many injured and arrested.
The world-renowned buyers later also called on the parties to resolve the dispute peacefully.
Sat Samuth, secretary of state at the Ministry of Labor, said he had not yet seen the letter from the retailer, but said the return to negotiations was not up to the ministry.
He was referring to a committee headed by Keat Chhon, announced by the prime minister last Friday:
Ken Loo, secretary-general of the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia, said the Garment Manufacturers Association, retailers and footwear association's request to return to the negotiating table was contrary to democratic principles.
Union leaders gathered Wednesday at a meeting in Phnom Penh, where they said a peaceful demonstration would resume if the government and employers did not return to the negotiating table.
According to the study, they claim that workers need about $ 160 to survive today instead of waiting for a gradual increase.
The meeting comes a day after Prime Minister Hun Sen said wages could not be raised to $ 160 and that the current $ 100 offer was better than any other country in the region.
Ath Thorn, president of the Confederation of Cambodian Garment Workers' Democratic Union, said at the meeting that the union could be flexible at any time.
Japanese direct investment down in 2013
A representative of the Japanese Embassy in Cambodia confirmed to the Post yesterday that the drop in investment was due to a sharp increase in investment in 2012, with one major project being the market. Modern Aeon Mall, and in general, such projects do not occur every year.
The Aeon Japan project has a total budget of up to $ 205 million.
Tayoshi Kiromiya, senior adviser at the Japanese Embassy in Cambodia, said Cambodia was competitive in terms of large and low labor costs, while labor costs in China, Thailand and other countries were high. Many of Japan's major investment destinations are growing.
The Japan External Trade Organization (JETRO) surveyed the earnings of Japanese factory workers in several countries in 2013, including the minimum wage, including allowances and overtime pay.
According to investment data from the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC), from 1994 to 2013, the amount of Japanese investment in Cambodia totaled $ 593 million, of which the investment volume in 2012 alone was more than half of the total. Total.
This data shows that Japanese investors ranked 11th among all foreign direct investment in Cambodia during that period.
Makoto Yachima, director general of Aeon Mall, expects that once the Japanese supermarket in Cambodia is completed and operational, it will contribute to attracting more Japanese investment to Cambodia.
Aeon Mall is located along Sothearos Street near the Russian Embassy in Cambodia and covers a total area of 68,000 square meters.
However, Kuromiya from the Japanese Embassy in Cambodia also warned that the current political crisis in Cambodia makes future forecasts of future Japanese investor flows questionable, as instability could hurt. To the decision of investors.
He said that for investors, stability is essential.
The signing ceremony of the grant agreement took place at the Ministry of Economy and Finance in the presence of Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Izaki Hiroshi, Chief Representative of JICA Cambodia.
National road infrastructure is important in facilitating economic growth and the provision of public services, especially in the context of regional economic integration.
The Government of Japan has been cooperating in the development of National Road No. 1 Phnom Penh Neak Loeung since 2005 with a total length of 56 km and a total value of approximately $ 86 million.
Mr. Izaki Hiroshi stated that in contributing to Cambodia's support for regional economic ties, the Japanese government has also helped improve National Road 5, an important part of the southern economic corridor and highway. ASEAN, which connects Phnom Penh and Bangkok.
The Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia (SECC) has decided in principle to allow Grand Twins International Cambodia to issue its first IPO on the Cambodian Stock Exchange.
According to a press release obtained by the Post yesterday, the decision is the result of the 27th meeting of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia held on January 9, 2013.
Grand Twin is the second company to receive an IPO on the Cambodia Securities Exchange after the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority.
Chhun Sambath, director of the Securities and Exchange Commission of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, told the Post yesterday that the granting of Grand Twins International Cambodia was possible in principle after a thorough evaluation by the SECC. Business, financial condition and profitability of the company and see that the company has sufficient conditions.
Since the launch of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, so far only one Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has traded.
The trading volume of PPWSA on Tuesday was 541 shares at 5,100 riel per share.
Sok Chamroeun, consulting director of Phnom Penh Securities, the securities underwriter of Grand Twin Cambodia, said that obtaining the SECC's principle of authorization would allow Grand Twins to conduct initial public offering to investors. Start selling shares to investors in early February.
A report to the Ho Chi Minh Stock Exchange released by the largest dairy company on Monday states that the Vietnamese Ministry of Planning and Investment has officially issued a foreign investment license to Vinamilk.
The dairy factory license was granted to Vinamilk on Monday by Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung during a visit to Cambodia.
The plant will produce 19 million liters of liquid milk, produce 64 million barrels of yogurt and 80 million cans of condensed milk annually, according to the statement.
Tran Tou, deputy commercial officer at the Vietnamese Embassy in Cambodia, praised the agreement, saying that while most of the process was automated, the new plant could provide 100 new jobs for Cambodians.
Vinamilk's license was obtained during the fourth Cambodia-Vietnam meeting on investment cooperation in Phnom Penh, in which Prime Minister Hun Sen said that Vietnamese investment in Cambodia increased by 250% between 2012 and 2013.
From 2009 to 2013, Vietnamese investment projects approved in Cambodia totaled $ 2.9 billion, said Deputy Minister of Planning and Investment Nguyen Thai Phuong on Monday.
Major Vietnamese investments focus on agriculture, forestry and energy.
Cambodia needs to maintain political stability for growth
The Asian Development Bank (ADB) said on Monday that low-income countries in Asia, such as Cambodia, should maintain political stability to capture the growth potential of developed and emerging Asian countries that are leading the global economy. .
He says many Asian countries are now facing electoral momentum.
So one of the privileges for them is political stability, as many Asian countries now have important elections.
Therefore, political stability should be a basis in Asian countries that should not miss this opportunity for development.
Cambodia held a general election on July 28 last year in which two major political parties were elected.
But the political stalemate remains as the opposition rejects the election results.
Since then, workers from the garment and textile industries, which account for about 70 percent of their exports, have been protesting for an increase in the minimum wage to $ 160 a month.
But the government has agreed to provide $ 100, which will take effect in January.
But he says there are issues that these countries should focus on in terms of looking at infrastructure, clean water, transportation and more.
These areas should be well managed, including regulatory.
So these economies can catch up with other developed countries and have more opportunities to do so while their population is young and labor force is low.
In October 2013, the ADB maintained its forecast for Cambodia's economic growth at 7.2 percent in 2013, driven by rising exports, growth in construction and services.
In 2014, growth is expected to reach 7.5 percent due to growth in Europe and the United States.
Cambodia's total foreign reserves rose 9.9 percent to $ 3.6 billion in the first half of 2013, equivalent to more than four months of imports and services.
This was stated by Prime Minister Hun Sen at the 4th Conference on Cambodia-Vietnam Investment Cooperation in Phnom Penh yesterday.
The Cambodia-Vietnam Investment Cooperation Conference was held at the Peace Palace yesterday in the presence of Prime Minister Hun Sen and Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung, as well as business representatives from both countries.
Deputy Minister of Planning and Investment Nguyen The Phuong said that the business activities of Vietnamese companies in Cambodia have increased significantly in both the number of investment projects and the amount of investment after the meeting on investment cooperation. This was done in Ho Chi Minh City in 2009.
From 2009-2013, Vietnamese investors received a total of 103 investment permits in Cambodia with an investment capital of $ 2.9 million.
For 2013, the total investment projects of Vietnamese companies in Cambodia are 19 projects.
According to The Phoeung, projects in which Vietnamese businessmen invest in Cambodia focus on agriculture and forestry, energy, finance, banking, insurance and telecommunications.
There are a number of Vietnamese investment projects underway, such as the Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Venture, Cho Ray Hospital, Phnom Penh, the five-star chemical fertilizer plant, the ethanol sugar plant, the power plant and the rubber plantation project.
Kith Meng, president of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, said yesterday that businessmen of the two countries were optimistic that the two countries' trade would reach $ 5 billion by 2015, the size of bilateral trade planned by the two governments. Achieved.
However, some remain skeptical of Vietnam's influence over the CPP-led Cambodian government.
The CNRP has repeatedly criticized and criticized the Cambodian government under Prime Minister Hun Sen for causing harm to Cambodia when it reached an agreement with Vietnam, and has always pushed for talks that focus on equal interests.
Sok Touch, an independent analyst, once confirmed to the Post that bilateral relations between Cambodia and Vietnam are currently unbalanced, as the Vietnamese government has taken great care to protect its indigenous people. Many in Cambodia.
Phnom Penh: Cambodia's total tax collection in 2013 was about 881 million dollars, an increase of about 16 percent from 2012.
This is according to the annual report of the General Department of Taxation.
According to the report, tax collection in 2013 increased all major tax categories.
Salary tax collection increased by 27%, business profit tax increased by 20%, VAT increased by 14% and special tax increased by 16%.
Din Virak, director of the VCPital Institute, who will be an economist, said that while growing tax collection, Cambodia needs to further strengthen the efficiency of internal tax collection, as it is necessary to maintain Balancing the national budget, while the trend of revenue from customs duties will be reduced in the coming years after the ASEAN economic integration in 2015.
He said tax revenue was an important source of state revenue, enabling the state to increase the salaries of civil servants, teachers and other public servants.
The report shows that revenue from tax collection from major business activities in 2013 increased in almost all activities.
Taxes on transportation and tourism increased by 34%, hotels and guesthouses increased by about 20%, garment manufacturing by 44%, financial services increased by 27%, airports and ports increased by about 82%, architecture and construction An increase of about 34.2 percent and some other activities also increased.
The Post tried to contact Chou Vichith, secretary of state at the Ministry of Economy and Finance, for further comment on the increase in tax collection in 2013, but could not be reached by telephone Sunday.
However, at last weekend's tax collection ceremony, Mr. Vichet hailed the positive results of the 2013 tax collection, and at the same time asked all tax officials to continue to overcome All challenges to perform the task of collecting all types of tax revenue in accordance with the target and increase the provision of services to taxpayers better.
$ 150 million project to start soon
A $ 150 million Paris-style building project on Diamond Island will begin in the coming months.
The project will take four years to build on 70,000 square meters.
While planning is still underway and a construction contract has not yet been issued, Touch Samnang, deputy director general of OCIC, told the Post that he had a vision of opening shops, apartments, condominiums and hotels to the public. People living in this new area.
Chrek Soknim, deputy general manager of Vtrust Real Estate, welcomed the project as the growing population of Phnom Penh and the lack of housing were a growing concern.
The report says:
Hotels for foreigners set up
Phnom Penh: The manager of the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone confirmed yesterday that a hotel for foreign investors and staff is being built in the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone (PPSEZ).
A press release from the company's annual report says:
HKL signed a $ 10 million loan agreement with German investment and development corporation DEG yesterday.
This is according to Mr. Huot Ieng Tong, General Director of Hattha Kaksekar Microfinance Institution.
Seeing the potential of small and medium enterprises in Cambodia, Huot Ieng Tong said his microfinance institution focused on promoting the SME sector by expanding lending into the sector.
Developing countries need the SME sector to grow in parallel.
We hope that more lending to the SME sector will help boost the economy.
While borrowing from foreign banks amid political instability, Huot Ieng Tong said it was a reflection of the stability of the Cambodian economy.
As a financier of private sector investment in developing countries and emerging markets for more than 50 years, DEG, a subsidiary of the German development bank KFW, is confident of Cambodia's future economic growth.
He was referring to the current loan rate of 12 percent.
Huot Ieng Tong claims to be able to offer competitive interest rates.
It depends on the negotiations and their business situation.
The higher the risk, the higher the interest rate.
Mfone lawyers ask court to speed up
Lawyers for Mfone, a Cambodian bankrupt telecommunications company, on Thursday sent a letter to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to expedite work on lawsuits against four of its debtors.
Khan Serey Vuthy, Ouk Ry's senior legal adviser and interim governor of Mfone, said:
Ouk Ry says the four debtors owed Mfone about $ 700,000 and are currently negotiating with us.
When we receive this money, we will pay the workers as our priority.
But he claims that so far the company has paid only $ 2.6 million.
We want them to speed up their payments as well.
Mfone assets are estimated at $ 105 million, but this is just the initial listing value of the assets, and the actual market value could be as high as $ 30 million to $ 40 million.
Factory Association plans to sue union
The Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia (GMAC) is helping its members sue a number of unions for damaging property following a demonstration demanding a $ 160 minimum wage increase.
Ken Loo, secretary-general of the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia, said more than 150 members would file complaints and that number was set to rise.
The association claims that the wage protests, which began in late December and are now quiet, have resulted in the factory losing more than $ 200 million in profits.
The six unions at the center of the conflict are the targets of legal action.
The unions could not be reached for comment on Tuesday.
Hundreds of factories were closed during a protest that sparked a spate of shootings by government armed forces that left four workers dead and several others injured on January 3 during a park protest. Canadia Industry.
Mr. Loo added that a number of lawsuits had already been filed, but did not specify the amount of damages to be claimed.
GMAC plans to sue were formally discussed by the Korean Trade Union Confederation on Monday in a show claiming South Korean garment factories would support the lawsuit.
The arrests took place outside a South Korean-owned garment factory on Thursday.
The administration of Canadia Industrial Park said on Tuesday that two South Korean companies were operating in the area.
But he says most are running their businesses and were not harmed during the protests.
I do not want to cause legal problems.
Luxury car sales up slightly
Sales of luxury cars in Cambodia rose slightly in 2013, the year of the election, as industry insiders expect a further increase this year.
Sales of Toyota Cambodia, the most popular Toyota dealer in the Cambodian market, reached more than 1,000 units in 2013, a slight increase from 2012.
This is according to Kong Nguon, CEO of Toyota Cambodia.
While sales have risen slightly, Kong Nguon expects to be able to sell up to 1,400 vehicles this year as Cambodia's economy continues to grow.
Nowadays, customers seem to be turning to new cars.
The company plans to import more new models to add options for family customers.
He said car sales rose 30 per cent year-on-year in 2013, a figure he said could be higher if there was enough supply.
We have not had a car for sale for a while.
He added that while the middle-income population is growing, including the growth of the Cambodian economy, more and more consumers are looking for more modern and aesthetically pleasing cars.
More and more people are now able to afford modern and new cars.
He said yesterday that the number of cars on sale had dropped by about 60 per cent compared to 2012.
But in the second half of the election, and after the election, until now, business has not been good due to the election and the massive protests.
He expressed concern about sales this year:
He was referring to the import of unofficial cars, which has caused unfair competition for licensed dealers.
We specialize in importing and we are a licensed distributor.
Senators yesterday agreed to enact a GI trademark law aimed at strengthening the scope of enforcement of intellectual property rights to protect the interests of producers and consumers of GI-branded goods.
This is according to a press release from the General Secretariat of the Senate yesterday.
GI trademark is a trademark that specifies the specific location of a product that is of a unique quality or has the most special recognition that the same product from another region can not have the same conditions. .
In Cambodia, there are two types of GI protected products: Kampot pepper and Kampong Speu palm sugar.
A press release from the General Secretariat of the Senate states:
According to the source, the law aims to protect the intellectual property of producers, operators and consumers of products bearing the brand name of the product, as well as to maintain national identity and strengthen traditional knowledge.
The Ministry of Commerce issued a proclamation in 2010 identifying the GI brand on Kampot pepper and Kampong Speu palm sugar, and this recognition has resulted in more orders for both products in both domestic and international markets. International.
Nguon Lay, president of the Kampot Pepper Association, told the Post yesterday that the decision to adopt the law on geographical indication would fully benefit Kampot pepper producers and Kampong Speu palm sugar producers who have received GI.
He said that the previous announcement from the Ministry of Commerce was small in scope compared to having clear rules, which led some traders to take pepper products from other regions and disguise them as GI products. .
Cambodia still has many potential products that can be registered to identify geographical brands.
Those products include Duren, Kampot, Prahok, Siem Reap, Mien, Pailin and many more agricultural products, but in order to be eligible for GI products, producers have to apply more complex production methods than conventional production in addition to the favorable geographical location they have.
The law will be sent to the King for signature and will be officially promulgated soon.
Palm Sugar Association signs agreement with Korea
The Kampong Speu Palm Sugar Development Association plans to sign an agreement to sell GI-certified palm sugar products with Korean business investment promotion agency KOTRA for export to Korea.
Sam Saroeun, president of the Kampong Speu Palm Sugar Development Association, told the Post yesterday that the deal was expected to begin in early February if authorities agreed to a request for 3,000 square meters. 16 villages in Samrong Tong and Odong districts for the construction of sanitary ware under KOTRA investment.
Farmers in each village will have to use the ovens as a whole to produce palm sugar.
The Korean company will only buy palm sugar produced in this sanitary ware.
The deal allows farmers to sell up to 300 tonnes of GI palm sugar to Korea a year.
However, he did not disclose the price of palm sugar to be exported.
The Kampong Speu Palm Sugar Development Association has 142 families producing palm sugar.
Six local companies are ordering and exporting GI palm sugar abroad, including Japan, the United States, France and the United Kingdom.
Farmers in Kampong Speu can produce 250 to 300 tonnes of palm sugar per year, while GI palm sugar demand for export is only 35 tonnes during the 2013 and 2014 harvests.
Hong Hoeung, director of the Palm Sugar Agricultural Development Community, hailed the deal, saying that through it, Kampong Speu palm sugar would be able to expand its market further.
Currently, palm sugar produced according to GI geographical standards costs 5,500 riel, while regular palm sugar costs 2,500 to 3,000 riel per kilogram.
However, he said the project to produce palm sugar in the sanitation plant could be difficult for some farmers.
Kampong Speu Palm Sugar received a GI certification in 2010 under the auspices of the World Trade Organization.
The draft law on geographical indication proposed by the Ministry of Commerce was approved by the Plenary Session of the Council of Ministers on November 8, 2013 and submitted to the Plenary Session of the National Assembly. From December 30, 2013.
The law aims to protect the intellectual property of producers, operators and consumers of products bearing the GI brand, as well as to maintain national identity and strengthen traditional knowledge and contribute to poverty reduction.
Intervention Buyers Drive Solutions
Buyers have urged the Cambodian government and stakeholders to resolve disputes in the garment industry over a peaceful minimum wage increase.
In the letter, buyers expressed grave concern over the tragic events of January 3, 2014, over protests to raise the minimum wage.
The letter said:
News of deaths and injuries on January 3 We call on all parties to exercise maximum restraint and stop the use of force or violence.
The buyers urge the government, the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia and all relevant unions to engage in fair and early negotiations to expedite the settlement of the dispute.
Promote and support the development of regular wage assessment date mechanisms as a basis for future peaceful wage negotiations.
The buyers say they are committed to Cambodia for the country's long-term economic development and for the prosperity of the Cambodian people.
Rong Chhun, president of the Cambodian Trade Union Confederation, said he applauded the buyer's intervention, saying it was a good thing for workers.
Rong Chhun said that if future talks still failed, protests would resume.
Van Sou Ieng, president of the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia, announced on Monday in response to the recent violence that orders from buyers would fall by between 20 and 30 per cent in 2014.
GMAC's announcement comes three days after government forces opened fire on garment workers during a protest that killed four workers.
Workers are demanding a minimum wage of $ 160.
ILO officials say the industry is still growing.
He said Cambodia's garment sector could grow by 20 percent over the next five years.
Consumer price index in November fell 0.3%
Phnom Penh: While many consumers have complained about rising commodity prices in the market after customs reforms since November 2013, a new report from the National Institute of Statistics shows that key consumer prices In November 2013, it was down 0.3 percent from October.
According to the National Institute of Statistics of the Ministry of Planning, food prices in November 2013 decreased by 0.6 percent compared to October 2013.
An official from the Ministry of Planning, who asked not to be named because he did not have permission to comment to the media, said the study was conducted to gather information from four major markets in Phnom Penh, including Deum Kor Or Russey, Phsar Thom Thmei and Phnom Penh. Chbar Ampov.
The average data on domestically produced main commodities, including rice, pork, chicken and fish, fell slightly from October.
The price of fish is also slightly lower due to the harvest season.
Many retailers made similar comments regarding the stabilization of some key domestic commodities between October and November.
But at the same time, they say the prices of almost all spices imported from neighboring countries have risen sharply since October.
Bunthoeun, a 51-year-old chicken trader at Boeung Keng Kang Market, said the price of chicken had not risen during the last two to three months, at around 14,000 riel per kilogram.
The prices of pork, fish and some locally produced vegetables have not changed much, she said.
Phnom Penh: Although the political situation in Cambodia is a bit murky, local investors have not hesitated, with the recent development of housing company Ly Hour Group decided to invest more than 100 million Dollars to build a semi-modern market and 280 flats along Street 598.
Ly Hour, CEO of Ly Hour Group, said at the groundbreaking ceremony for the project on Saturday at Phnom Penh's Borey Vimean, located along 598 Chea Sophara Street, that the current political situation was not adversely affected. To your investment.
I think political disputes will be resolved.
At the beginning, everything was done at once, with this project we built a market and an apartment at the same time.
The new project will be built on more than 4 hectares of land and is scheduled to take 24 months to build at a cost of more than $ 100 million.
This is the third phase of Borey Vimean Phnom Penh, where the company will build a semi-modern market with three floors and a fourth floor as a cinema, as well as 280 apartments.
Mr. Ly Hour said that after the election, some Boreys had problems selling, while the sales of Borey Vimean Phnom Penh went better than usual because the construction of Borey Vimean Phnom Penh is focused on quality, while the architectural style is good. Modern and up-to-date with the right technical specifications.
Po Eav Kong, general manager of Asia Real Estate, said some local investors were following the political developments in Cambodia, while some Borey houses were not selling as fast as they had during the period. No vote.
He said that at present, the movement of buying and selling and investing is still there, but only in small quantities.
Dith Channa, General Manager of VMC Real Estate, said:
Factory industry loses nearly $ 300 million
The garment industry in Cambodia has lost nearly $ 300 million during the workers' strike, demanding a $ 160 wage increase.
Van Sou Ieng, president of the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia, said the industry had lost about $ 200 million in sales and another $ 70 million in investment in garment products lost to other garment-producing countries over the years. 15 days ago.
In addition to the loss of profits, orders could fall by 20 to 30 per cent this year, he said at a presentation at the Phnom Penh Hotel yesterday.
