Business situation in Canadia Park is calm
Every weekend, a main street in the Canadia Industrial Park, lined with garment factories, is bustling with workers.
The Canadia Industrial Park, which is home to more than 40 factories and more than 13,000 regular workers, has helped create hundreds of jobs for businesses in the area.
Every day, especially on holidays, daily grocery stalls and grocery stores are bustling with people shopping.
But things have changed dramatically since Friday, January 3, when four people were shot dead in a crackdown by authorities.
