The protest took place on motorbikes and tuk-tuks and lasted for about two hours in front of the Ministry of Economy, where protesters made verbal requests, with loudspeakers calling for the ministry to intervene to lower gas prices.
Vorn Pov, president of the Independent Democratic Association of Informal Economy and leader of the petrol-lowering protest, said the protest was attended by more than a thousand people.
